Taxonomy: US GAAP 2026
**/


rule-name-prefix DQC

/** V32 Release **/
/**

Overview: Business Development Companies (BDCs) and other investment companies report each investment on the Schedule of Investments (SOI) using an identifier axis.  Each member on the identifier axis identifies an individual investment or contract. Filers have been tagging the Schedule of Investments using tables that do not include an identifier axis, instead identifying investments using other axes such as the InvestmentIssuerNameAxis, InvestmentTypeAxis or an extension axis. When this occurs the individual investments cannot be identified.

The US GAAP taxonomy defines the following tables and the identifier axis used with each table:

Table                                       Identifier Axis
ScheduleOfInvestmentsTable                  InvestmentIdentifierAxis
InvestmentsSoldNotYetPurchasedTable         SecuritySoldShortIdentifierAxis
OpenOptionContractsWrittenTable             OpenOptionContractIdentifierAxis
OpenFuturesContractTable                    OpenFuturesContractIdentifierAxis
OpenForwardForeignCurrencyContractTable     OpenForwardForeignCurrencyContractIdentifierAxis
OpenSwapContractTable                       OpenSwapContractIdentifierAxis

Rule US.0252.10967 checks that the ScheduleOfInvestmentsTable includes the InvestmentIdentifierAxis.

Rule US.0252.10968 checks that the InvestmentsSoldNotYetPurchasedTable includes the SecuritySoldShortIdentifierAxis.

Rule US.0252.10969 checks that the OpenOptionContractsWrittenTable includes the OpenOptionContractIdentifierAxis.

Rule US.0252.10970 checks that the OpenFuturesContractTable includes the OpenFuturesContractIdentifierAxis.

Rule US.0252.10971 checks that the OpenForwardForeignCurrencyContractTable includes the OpenForwardForeignCurrencyContractIdentifierAxis.

Rule US.0252.10972 checks that the OpenSwapContractTable includes the OpenSwapContractIdentifierAxis.

Each assertion only evaluates tables in a statement section (role description contains '- Statement -') that is not parenthetical and that has facts reported in it.

Rule DQC.US.0210 is superseded by this rule that checks that the individual investment facts (interest rate, spread and floor) are reported with the InvestmentIdentifierAxis.

**/

ASSERT US.0252.10967 SATISFIED

$rule_id = (rule-name().split('.'))[rule-name().split('.').length];

/** DQCRT RULE **/
if not applicable_form(rule-name()) and not $BDC_FLAG
	skip
else

for $cube in soi_statement_cubes(ScheduleOfInvestmentsTable)
	$cubeDimensions = $cube.dimensions.concept.name

	/** Only evaluate a table that has facts reported in it **/
	$cubeFacts = list({covered @cube = $cube})
	$investmentIdentifierFacts = list({covered @InvestmentIdentifierAxis=*}).length == 0

	$cubeFacts.length > 0 and InvestmentIdentifierAxis not in $cubeDimensions and $investmentIdentifierFacts

message
"The Schedule of Investments in the section \"{$cube.drs-role.description}\" uses the ScheduleOfInvestmentsTable with the following axes: {$cubeDimensions.sort.join(', ')}.  This table does not include the InvestmentIdentifierAxis.  Each investment reported in the Schedule of Investments should be identified using a member on the InvestmentIdentifierAxis so that the attributes of each individual investment such as the cost, fair value, principal amount, interest rate and maturity can be identified. Please add the InvestmentIdentifierAxis to the table and report each investment using a member on this axis. If the table reflects a different investment type change the table name to the appropriate table concept that is used with that investment type and dimension.

Rule Element Id:{$rule_id}
Rule version: {$ruleVersion}"

severity error

effectiveDate $effective_dates[$rule_id]


