else

for $cube in soi_statement_cubes(InvestmentsSoldNotYetPurchasedTable)
	$cubeDimensions = $cube.dimensions.concept.name

	/** Only evaluate a table that has facts reported in it **/
	$cubeFacts = list({covered @cube = $cube})
	$investmentIdentifierFacts = list({covered @SecuritySoldShortIdentifierAxis=*}).length == 0

	$cubeFacts.length > 0 and SecuritySoldShortIdentifierAxis not in $cubeDimensions and $investmentIdentifierFacts

message
"The schedule of securities sold short in the section \"{$cube.drs-role.description}\" uses the InvestmentsSoldNotYetPurchasedTable with the following axes: {$cubeDimensions.sort.join(', ')}.  This table does not include the SecuritySoldShortIdentifierAxis.  Each security sold short should be identified using a member on the SecuritySoldShortIdentifierAxis so that the attributes of each individual security can be identified. Please add the SecuritySoldShortIdentifierAxis and report each security sold short using a member on this axis if this is the actual Investments sold not yet purchased table.  If the table reflects a different investment type change the table name to the appropriate table concept that is used with that investment type and dimension.

Rule Element Id:{$rule_id}
Rule version: {$ruleVersion}"

severity error

effectiveDate $effective_dates[$rule_id]


